  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_cd074933190d49c8b5e57ac775c566e0",
      "statement": "The webhook entrypoint is WebhookEngine.sendIncomingSmsWebhook(context, sms), called from IncomingMessageDispatcher.dispatch — the single fan-out for inbound SMS/MMS — after the Room shadow mirror and the blocklist check (the dispatcher is the only caller), so webhook dispatch always reflects provider-persisted message state, runs exactly once per delivered message (SmsReceiver dedupes SMS_RECEIVED against SMS_DELIVER; MMS arrives once via mmslib's MmsReceiver), and MMS is included through the same path.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/src/main/java/com/autonomousone/messages/gateway/WebhookEngine.kt#L20-L47",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:49b5ad76d5b007f8ef4eaee2ef309237fd60f933dadeb6e5d329550780bb0f50:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/src/main/java/com/autonomousone/messages/receiver/IncomingMessageDispatcher.kt#L68-L69",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0c79091c6613833e411a556d48931e96f5e0ec54fd3026f3c3032afea89604a5:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_c8cfc7e53b8647b0816b09ccfbfe784f",
      "statement": "Messages from blocked senders never reach the webhook entrypoint: IncomingMessageDispatcher returns silently (no bus event, no notification, row still persisted) before calling WebhookEngine.sendIncomingSmsWebhook, so blocked senders produce no webhooks by construction rather than by receiver-side filtering.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/src/main/java/com/autonomousone/messages/receiver/IncomingMessageDispatcher.kt#L54-L58",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:980b8613a77e3b849a6811235ea1f8ab579015ed95f32299ca2d744e79cf8776:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_aec99f37d52b41c8be39dafafe3e38c2",
      "statement": "Both outbound legs (local HTTPS webhook and cloud event upload) are gated by one check at the WebhookEngine entry — GatewayAccessPolicy.canTransmit(prefs.hasGatewayConsent, prefs.isEnabled), i.e. versioned consent AND the supervisor-derived runtime isEnabled flag — and when it fails all SMS dispatch is skipped together; there is no partial dispatch of one leg without the other.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/src/main/java/com/autonomousone/messages/gateway/GatewayAccessPolicy.kt#L3-L6",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3f67674d766a6e07f50363e9e321df1cacef5acb6e511bade22ef79993c38e2c:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/src/main/java/com/autonomousone/messages/gateway/WebhookEngine.kt#L28-L33",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3ab37e5b38afa19b0517834977a37f9c8464e7084bd9bcd91a992f317abcb5d5:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_83c7e173307f4a1b83904980ab60215e",
      "statement": "Gateway consent is versioned: hasGatewayConsent is true only when the stored consent version is >= CURRENT_CONSENT_VERSION (currently 1), so material data-use changes force a fresh opt-in before any webhook or cloud event is dispatched.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/src/main/java/com/autonomousone/messages/gateway/GatewayPreferences.kt#L127-L139",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:be4c2730903b497de4ddab91f281835839c9f67f193ba0b3d264d7b211d55bd0:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/src/main/java/com/autonomousone/messages/gateway/GatewayPreferences.kt#L51-L51",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b4f1286d10626ee0488cda9fd0b7da24213148b78b594a054d39db21e13c4181:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_304f6a27032b4304bea12e1d5e06ed58",
      "statement": "Both dispatches are fire-and-forget: each is launched as an independent coroutine on WebhookEngine's private CoroutineScope(SupervisorJob() + Dispatchers.IO); the local webhook's HTTP response code is read only to be logged and exceptions are caught and logged, so webhook or cloud-backend failures can never block or fail the SMS receiver.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/src/main/java/com/autonomousone/messages/gateway/WebhookEngine.kt#L15-L47",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0218da5eb5909e3358a330be15f443d57d314a3a1a035cb9c4d0657d1600fa42:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/src/main/java/com/autonomousone/messages/gateway/WebhookEngine.kt#L82-L89",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c98059a28edd67df5106b673367bcf16b42a9fd40e137b56f1ea98618cd85ecf:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_0aabb42a36624a58bbcb940bf657df60",
      "statement": "The local webhook body is a fixed five-field JSON object: event (always the literal \"sms_received\"), sender (originating address), message (full body), timestamp (sms.date in Unix epoch milliseconds), and threadId; the schema is WebhookPayload in docs/api/openapi.yaml.",
      "evidence": [
