    {
      "id": "claim_2d70839e33284b35904380fdea2b9bed",
      "statement": "The cloud event's eventId is a deterministic UUID derived as UUID.nameUUIDFromBytes of '<sender>|<date>|<message truncated to first 100 chars>', so the same SMS re-derived after a process restart or by two processes yields the same ID and the backend can safely deduplicate replays on that field.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/src/main/java/com/autonomousone/messages/gateway/WebhookEngine.kt#L146-L154",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:59b96a020ae511b50ea860cfd68d1819b67fba83bc4a8021bee36e456f71ddca:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d9dbe7b9c8314e4785f41c97cced618c",
      "statement": "Before uploading, sendCloudEvent checks GatewayPreferences.hasEventBeenSent(eventId) and skips events the backend already acknowledged; only a 2xx leads to markEventSent; on any failure the ID is not cached, but since SMS_DELIVER fires once there is no app-side replay — a permanently-down backend means the event is effectively lost, with backend-side retry expected to handle downstream delivery.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/src/main/java/com/autonomousone/messages/gateway/WebhookEngine.kt#L109-L143",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d9eef4490ffd4947cb0c5868bc99422b02df7f0393f46d19a476aabbb84d3e9f:"
        }
      ]
