    {
      "id": "claim_f064e336732d48c0a1bcc25e593e1aef",
      "statement": "The webhook signing secret is stored Keystore-encrypted (enc:v1: prefix via SecureStore) with legacy plaintext re-encrypted on first read, and persistence is fail-closed: storeEncrypted throws when the Android Keystore is unavailable instead of degrading to plaintext, so a dead Keystore manifests as an empty/blank secret (unsigned webhook or skipped cloud leg) rather than a plaintext secret leak.",
      "evidence": [
